  "title": "Introibo ad altare Dei.",
  "html_source": "<p>Latin for:</p><p>“I will go up to the altar of God.” – from <a href=\"https://genius.com/4603832\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\">Psalms 43:4</a></p><p>The line makes explicit that <a href=\"https://genius.com/1685453\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\">the opening scene</a> is a parody of Roman Catholic mass.</p><p>Also hints at a parody of ‘the Odyssey’ which, as epics conventionally did, opens with an invocation of the Muse, the daughter of Zeus.</p>",
